# meet capacity — DELIBERATELY PINNED TO ONE INSTANCE.
#
# ⚠️  Do not raise MaxSize above 1 until the concierge stores move out of process.
#
# `lib/concierge/bot-room-claim-store.ts`, `bot-start-lock-store.ts` and
# `bot-requests-store.ts` are plain Maps hung off `globalThis`. They are not
# shared, not persisted, and not coordinated. With two instances behind the load
# balancer:
#   - the "one bot per room" claim is enforced per-instance, so two requests
#     landing on different instances both succeed → two bots in one meeting;
#   - the start mutex protects nothing across instances;
#   - LiveKit webhooks reconcile whichever instance happens to receive them.
#
# That is a correctness failure, not a capacity limit — it gets worse under load,
# which is exactly when it would be introduced. MaxSize: 1 is the only thing
# currently preventing it. See docs/scale-readiness-plan.md (C6).
#
# Vertical scaling is safe and is what this file does: c6i.large is fixed
# performance rather than burstable, removing the CPU-credit cliff. Note that any
# instance replacement (including this one) restarts the process and therefore
# clears all in-memory claims, stranding sessions in flight — a pre-existing
# property of every meet deploy, not something introduced here.

option_settings:
  aws:autoscaling:launchconfiguration:
    InstanceType: c6i.large

  aws:autoscaling:asg:
    MinSize: 1
    MaxSize: 1
